.TH I_FLAGS 1 9/9/92
.CM 1
.SH NAME
Flags \- generate compiler options as needed by CS make
.SH SYNOPSIS
Flags I PATH_name
Flags L PATH_name
.SH DESCRIPTION
"Flags" is a cover for compilers that do not have the CMU CS frontend,
nor can or want to use the CMU cpp. Is is invoked in a compilation rule like
.I cc `Flags I MAKECPP CPATH`
to sort the same effects as using the CMU cpp as far as searching for
includes goes.

The CMU linker also searches its objects along the predefined LPATH search
list.  You can sort the same effect with a command line like
.I cc `Flags L LPATH`
.PP
.SH FILES
Makefile, makefile
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cc(1), cpp(1), ld(1)
